    "whole_relationship": "Three close photographic passages at the left follow supporting a plant, touching its rootball/soil, and an established planted result. The visual rhythm is made by working hands and material contacts rather than leaf decoration. A right-hand readable column links the grower story to the real visit and care offer.",
    "positive_direction": "Tactile monochrome documentary photography, silver highlights and deep charcoal shadows. Use deliberately different crop distances, fine controlled grain, real skin creases, soil particles and roots; focus follows contact rather than decorative blur. A large firm modern Korean sans Title and crisp regular body give the photographic sequence a direct, assured voice. Retain midtone detail and clean hand anatomy rather than crushed black silhouettes. Edit close observations of plant work: two hands support a small pot/rootball, fingers release soil around roots, and a grown plant sits stably in its pot. Show actual physical contacts and connected roots, not an illustrated hand icon or pseudo-archival stamps. These are three visual moments of the supplied caring theme, without adding a printed timetable or claiming a real person/place.",
